WEB FAMILY IDENTITY — LOOK, FEEL, AND READ THE SAME

\================================================================================



Shared visual system (legal.css contract)

\- Every product legal/support site uses legal.css with
the same design tokens:

  - Max content
width \~760px, centered; system font stack (Segoe UI, system-ui).

  - CSS
variables: --bg, --panel, --text, --muted, --border, --link.

  - .panel —
white card with border and 8px radius; .legal-prose for body copy.

  -
.philosophy-banner — highlighted local-first callout (support page).

  - .site-footer
— minimal copyright footer; not a wall of links on every page.

\- Utility-first density: short sections, h2 headings,
bullet lists — easy to scan on phone and desktop.

\- No hero images, animation, or decorative marketing
layouts on privacy, terms, or support pages.

\- philosophy-tagline on key pages when accurate:
“Local-first · No Nivo78 account · No cloud sync · No analytics”

  (adapt only
when the product’s job explicitly requires an account or optional sync — state
the exception plainly).



Shared page structure (every legal/support HTML page)

\- \<html lang="en">, charset UTF-8,
viewport meta for mobile.

\- \<head> SEO (mandatory): unique title; meta
description (\~160 characters); meta robots; meta author;

  link
rel="canonical" (exact page URL); Open Graph (title, description,
url, site\_name, locale);

  Twitter card
(summary or summary\_large\_image). See WEB SEO section for hosted PHP
(n78\_seo\_head.php).

\- \<main class="app"> wrapper.

\- Header: optional eyebrow back link (← {Product}
Support or ← Nivo78) → h1 page title → subtitle.

\- Privacy page header (required on every privacy
policy — in-repo HTML and hosted equivalent):

  - MUST match
the Privacy policy first two lines contract above (shared CSS + markup).

  - Line 3 when
present: Local-first philosophy-tagline below the product name.

\- Body: one or more \<article class="panel
legal-prose"> (support may add philosophy-banner panel first).

\- Footer: \<footer class="site-footer">
with © Nivo78 Mobile Apps, LLC — on support, privacy, and terms pages.

\- link rel="stylesheet"
href="../legal.css" (or ./legal.css on index as appropriate).





\================================================================================

WEB NAVIGATION, FOOTERS, AND LEGAL PLACEMENT

\================================================================================



Same five destinations as the app (labels and URLs
must match)

\- Help         
— support center / knowledge base at https\://nivo78.com/{product}/support/

\- Feedback     
— support page explains Help → Feedback in app;
mailto\:feedback\@nivo78.com with subject hint

\- Support center — support/index.html (and hosted KB
when exported)

\- Privacy      
— privacy/index.html

\- Terms        
— terms/index.html



Placement rules (web)

\- Product index (code/Website/{product}/index.html):
Legal & support section lists Privacy, Terms, Support center.

\- Support page: Contact block (support, feedback,
contact mailto links) + Legal section (Privacy, Terms links).

\- Privacy page: cross-link to Support for
user-friendly security overview; link to Terms in contact block.

\- Privacy page header: h1 “Privacy Policy” + prominent
p.policy-product-name (public product name).

\- Terms page: link to Privacy in agreement section;
eyebrow back to Support.

\- Store listings (Partner Center, Play Console, App
Store Connect) use the same privacy and terms URLs as in-app links.



Voluntary Tip Jar for free utilities (WEB-FREE-APP-TIP-JAR)

\- Mandatory for all free Nivo78 apps (utilities with no paid tier, license, or in-app billing):

  1. Product hub (index.html / index.php): "Support Nivo78 (Voluntary Tip Jar)" entry in Legal & support list, plus a dedicated .n78-tip-jar-panel card with standard Nivo78 blue highlight stripe (border-top: 4px solid var(--n78-accent)), synergy badge, and "☕ Buy the developer a coffee" button (https\://buymeacoffee.com/nivo78).

  2. Support center (support/index.html / support/index.php): dedicated .n78-tip-jar-panel section immediately above Contact, plus a bullet under Contact ("Voluntary support: Buy the developer a coffee (Tip Jar)").

\- Hard rule — NO in-app donation or tip links:

  - Do NOT place tip jar, coffee, or donation buttons inside the store application binary. Out-of-band payment links inside store apps violate app store commerce policies (Microsoft Store, Google Play, Apple App Store) and risk store certification rejection.

  - The tip jar lives exclusively on the website, discoverable naturally through Support center web navigation.

\- Honest scope guarantee: The app remains 100% free with no locked features, no paywalls, and no nags. Tips are strictly voluntary.



Footer content (web)

\- site-footer: copyright line only on legal pages — “©
{year} Nivo78 Mobile Apps, LLC. All rights reserved.”

  (no city on
the web site-footer copyright line; workflow-style clutter belongs on product
marketing pages, not privacy/terms).

\- Entity block on privacy/terms/support contact
sections: Nivo78 Mobile Apps, LLC, then Tyler, Texas (city lives here on the
web).

\- Do not embed web forms that upload user project
data, attachments, or diagnostics — contact is mailto-only.





\================================================================================

WEB CONTACT, FEEDBACK, AND SUPPORT — SAME INTERFACE
CONTRACT

\================================================================================



Support page Contact section (required)

\- Support:  
mailto\:support\@nivo78.com — general help and licensing

\- Feedback: 
MUST state bug reports use Help → Feedback in the app (only path with
automatic diagnostics);

             MAY
offer mailto\:feedback\@nivo78.com for Help and feature ideas — plain note that
web email

            
includes only what the user writes (no automatic version, page, or audit
context)

\- Contact:  
mailto\:contact\@nivo78.com — business and general contact, not primary
bug triage



Copy must match app Feedback contract and
device-vs-web routing (v1.6)

\- Web email contains only what the user writes — no
automatic attachment of project files, vault, passwords, or diagnostics.

\- Bug reports: support page and KB MUST direct users
to in-app Help → Feedback; explain why (version, active page, checklist
context, redacted audit lines).

\- Help and feature request: web mailto is acceptable;
KB may mention support@ or feedback@ with subject prefix.

\- Do not promise web-based bug submission, silent log
upload, or contact forms that collect diagnostics — web stays mailto or points
to in-app Feedback for bugs.

\- Verify script or release gate SHOULD check support
HTML for in-app bug-report routing markers (see product verify script).



Support center vs marketing product page

\- support/index.html — security overview, platforms,
encrypted vs plain summary, contact, legal links.

\- Hosted product page (nivo78.com/{product}/) may
carry audience and feature copy — must still agree with support/privacy on data
handling and limits.

\- Help KB articles (when used) export from
engine/registry copy via updocs — same plain language as in-app Help.





